I can provide the complete code and explanations for both parts of your original question.

**Part 1: Maximum Profit from Selling Stock with Buy**

Given a list of prices where each price is known at the time of purchase, calculate the maximum profit that can be achieved by selling the stock at any point.

```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[][] prices = {{10, 6}, {15, 12}};

        System.out.println(maxProfit(prices));
    }

    public static int maxProfit(int[][] prices) {
        if (prices.length < 2) return 0;

        int n = prices[0].length;
        int[] dp1 = new int[n];
        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
            int minPrice = Integer.MAX_VALUE;
            for (int j = 0; j <= i; j++) {
                if (prices[j][i] < minPrice) minPrice = prices[j][i];
                dp1[i] = Math.max(dp1[i], dp1[j] + minPrice - prices[i][i]);
            }
        }

        return dp1[n - 1];
    }

    public static double maxProfit(double[][] pricesDbl) {
        if (pricesDbl.length < 2) return 0;

        int n = pricesDbl[0].length;
        double[] dp1 = new double[n];
        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
            double minPrice = Double.MAX_VALUE;
            for (int j = 0; j <= i; j++) {
                if (pricesDbl[j][i] < minPrice) minPrice = pricesDbl[j][i];
                dp1[i] = Math.max(dp1[i], dp1[j] + minPrice - pricesDbl[i][i]);
            }
        }

        return dp1[n - 1];
    }
}
```

**Part 2: Maximum Profit from Selling Stock with Multiple Prices**

Given a list of prices where each price is known at the time of purchase, calculate the maximum profit that can be achieved by selling the stock at any point.

```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[][] prices = {{10, 6}, {15, 12}};

        System.out.println(maxProfitMultiplePrices(prices));
    }

    public static int maxProfit(int[][] prices) {
        if (prices.length < 2) return 0;

        int n = prices[0].length;
        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j <= i; j++) {
                if (prices[j][i] > prices[i][i]) {
                    prices[j][i] = prices[i][i];
                }
            }
        }

        return maxProfit(prices);
    }

    public static int maxProfitMultiplePrices(int[][] prices) {
        if (prices.length < 2) return 0;

        int n = prices[0].length;
        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
            int minPrice = Integer.MAX_VALUE;
            for (int j = 0; j <= i; j++) {
                if (j == 0 || prices[j][i] > prices[j - 1][i]) {
                    minPrice = Math.min(minPrice, prices[j][i]);
                } else {
                    minPrice = prices[j - 1][i];
                }
            }

            for (int j = 0; j < i; j++) {
                if (j == 0 || prices[i][j] > prices[i - 1][j]) {
                    prices[i][j] = prices[i - 1][j];
                } else {
                    prices[i][j] += minPrice - prices[i - 1][j];
                }
            }

            System.out.println(Arrays.toString(prices));
        }

        return maxProfit(prices);
    }

    public static int maxProfit(int[][] prices) {
        for (int i = 0; i < prices.length; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j <= i; j++) {
                if (prices[j][i] > prices[i][j]) {
                    prices[j][i] = prices[i][j];
                }
            }
        }

        return Arrays.stream(prices).max().getAsInt();
    }

    public static double maxProfit(double[][] pricesDbl) {
        for (int i = 0; i < pricesDbl.length; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j <= i; j++) {
                if (pricesDbl[j][i] > pricesDbl[i][j]) {
                    pricesDbl[j][i] = pricesDbl[i][j];
                }
            }
        }

        return Arrays.stream(pricesDbl).max().getAsDouble();
    }
}
```

Note: The above solutions have a time complexity of O(n^2) and space complexity of O(1), where n is the number of prices.
