**Part 1: Maximum Profit from Selling Stock with Multiple Prices**

Given a list of prices where each price is known at the time of purchase, calculate the maximum profit that can be achieved by selling the stock at any point.

```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[][] prices = {{10, 6}, {15, 12}};

        System.out.println(maxProfitMultiplePrices(prices));
    }

    public static int maxProfit(int[][] prices) {
        if (prices.length < 2) return 0;

        for (int i = 1; i < prices[0].length; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j <= i; j++) {
                if (prices[j][i] > prices[i][i]) {
                    prices[j][i] = prices[i][i];
                }
            }
        }

        return maxProfit(prices);
    }

    public static int maxProfit(int[][] prices) {
        int n = prices[0].length;
        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
            int minPrice = Integer.MAX_VALUE;
            for (int j = 0; j <= i; j++) {
                if (prices[j][i] > minPrice) {
                    minPrice = prices[j][i];
                }
            }

            for (int j = 1; j < n; j++) {
                if (j == i || prices[i][j] >= minPrice) continue;
                prices[i][j] += minPrice - prices[i-1][j];
            }
        }

        return maxProfit(prices);
    }
}
```

**Part 2: Maximum Profit from Selling Stock with Multiple Prices**

Given a list of prices where each price is known at the time of purchase, calculate the maximum profit that can be achieved by selling the stock at any point.

```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[][] prices = {{10, 6}, {15, 12}};

        System.out.println(maxProfitMultiplePrices(prices));
    }

    public static int maxProfit(int[][] prices) {
        if (prices.length < 2) return 0;

        for (int i = 1; i < prices[0].length; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j <= i; j++) {
                if (j == 0 || prices[j][i] > prices[j - 1][i]) {
                    prices[j][i] = prices[j - 1][i];
                } else {
                    prices[j][i] += prices[j - 1][i] - prices[j][i];
                }
            }
        }

        return maxProfit(prices);
    }

    public static int maxProfit(int[][] prices) {
        if (prices.length < 2) return 0;

        int n = prices[0].length;
        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
            if (i == 1 || prices[i][i] > prices[i-1][i]) {
                prices[i][i] += prices[i - 1][i];
            } else {
                for (int j = 0; j <= i; j++) {
                    if (j == 0 || prices[j][i] > prices[j - 1][i]) {
                        prices[j][i] = prices[j - 1][i];
                    } else {
                        prices[j][i] += prices[j - 1][i] - prices[j][i];
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        int maxProfit = Integer.MIN_VALUE;
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            if (i == 0 || prices[i][n-1] > prices[i - 1][n-1]) {
                maxProfit = Math.max(maxProfit, prices[i][n-1]);
            } else {
                maxProfit += prices[i][n-1] - prices[i - 1][n-1];
            }
        }

        return maxProfit;
    }
}
```

Note: The above solutions have a time complexity of O(n^2) and space complexity of O(1), where n is the number of prices.
