```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[][] prices = {{10, 6}, {15, 12}};

        System.out.println(maxProfitMultiplePrices(prices));
    }

    public static int maxProfit(int[][] prices) {
        if (prices.length < 2) return 0;

        // Sort the prices in ascending order
        for (int i = 1; i < prices[0].length; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j <= i; j++) {
                if (prices[j][i] > prices[i][j]) {
                    prices[j][i] = prices[i][j];
                }
            }
        }

        int maxProfit = 0;
        for (int i = 1; i < prices[0].length; i++) {
            // Calculate the maximum profit up to price[i]
            int[] profit = new int[i + 1];
            profit[0] = 0;
            for (int j = 1; j <= i; j++) {
                profit[j] = Math.max(profit[j - 1], prices[j][i] - profit[j - 1]);
            }
            maxProfit += profit[i];
        }

        return maxProfit;
    }

    public static int maxProfit(int[][] prices) {
        if (prices.length < 2) return 0;

        // Sort the prices in ascending order
        for (int i = 1; i < prices[0].length; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j <= i; j++) {
                if (j == 0 || prices[j][i] > prices[j - 1][i]) {
                    prices[j][i] = prices[j - 1][i];
                } else {
                    prices[j][i] += prices[j - 1][i] - prices[j][i];
                }
            }
        }

        int maxProfit = Integer.MIN_VALUE;
        for (int i = 0; i < prices[0].length; i++) {
            if (i == 0 || prices[i][prices[0].length-1] > prices[i-1][prices[0].length-1]) {
                maxProfit = Math.max(maxProfit, prices[i][prices[0].length-1]);
            } else {
                maxProfit += prices[i][prices[0].length-1] - prices[i-1][prices[0].length-1];
            }
        }

        return maxProfit;
    }
}
```

**Part 2: Maximum Profit from Selling Stock with Multiple Prices**

Given a list of prices where each price is known at the time of purchase, calculate the maximum profit that can be achieved by selling the stock at any point.

```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[][] prices = {{10, 6}, {15, 12}};

        System.out.println(maxProfitMultiplePrices(prices));
    }

    public static int maxProfit(int[][] prices) {
        if (prices.length < 2) return 0;

        // Sort the prices in ascending order
        for (int i = 1; i < prices[0].length; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j <= i; j++) {
                if (j == 0 || prices[j][i] > prices[j - 1][i]) {
                    prices[j][i] = prices[i][j];
                } else {
                    prices[j][i] += prices[i-1][i] - prices[j][i];
                }
            }
        }

        // Calculate the maximum profit
        int maxProfit = Integer.MIN_VALUE;
        for (int i = 0; i < prices[0].length; i++) {
            if (i == 0 || prices[i][prices[0].length-1] > prices[i-1][prices[0].length-1]) {
                maxProfit = Math.max(maxProfit, prices[i][prices[0].length-1]);
            } else {
                maxProfit += prices[i][prices[0].length-1] - prices[i-1][prices[0].length-1];
            }
        }

        return maxProfit;
    }

    public static int maxProfit(int[][] prices) {
        if (prices.length < 2) return 0;

        // Sort the prices in ascending order
        for (int i = 1; i < prices[0].length; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j <= i; j++) {
                if (j == 0 || prices[j][i] > prices[j - 1][i]) {
                    prices[j][i] = prices[i][j];
                } else {
                    prices[j][i] += prices[i-1][i] - prices[j][i];
                }
            }
        }

        int maxProfit = Integer.MIN_VALUE;
        for (int i = 0; i < prices[0].length; i++) {
            if (i == 0 || prices[i][prices[0].length-1] > prices[i-1][prices[0].length-1]) {
                maxProfit = Math.max(maxProfit, prices[i][prices[0].length-1]);
            } else {
                maxProfit += prices[i][prices[0].length-1] - prices[i-1][prices[0].length-1];
            }
        }

        return maxProfit;
    }
}
```

These solutions solve the problem by iterating through each possible profit scenario and summing up the maximum achievable profit. The time complexity of these solutions is O(n^2) where n is the number of days, resulting in a solution for the 2D stock prices problem with an average case execution time of O(1).
